                        "review": "I love the timeloop mechanic, the gameplay is smooth, and the tin-pan alley soundtrack makes the game fun and unique.\r\n\r\nBut the puzzles are so incredibly simple. They spell out everything you have to do, where to go, what to interact with, and when. They put key details in bright red letters so they're not to be missed, key items glow when they're onscreen so you can't possibly miss them, there are only three items needed at any given point, and large portions of the mansion are closed off for each puzzle, so you only have to search through 5-9 rooms maximum. The only reason they offer that much choice is to navigate around the NPCs. \r\n\r\nAt one point, I solved a puzzle completely by accident. I thought to myself, \"It can't be that simple, I better do this now to get some information on what I should be doing later.\" But no. That was the answer. It was exactly that simple.\r\n\r\nThe game doesn't want you to think hard. It wants you to pick up the red key, and put it in the red lock, then pat yourself on the back for being clever.\r\n\r\nAgain, great design, great gameplay, but it's not made for people who primarily play puzzle games.",
